cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the BiLSTM-BAN base-model preprint listed under references."
title: "TEMA-ENM: An Interpretable Attention-Topology Framework Decouples Affinity and Efficacy from Sequence Alone"
abstract: >-
  TEMA-ENM is an interpretable deep transfer-learning framework that decouples
  binding affinity from signaling efficacy using a bilinear attention network,
  from protein sequence alone. Starting from the pre-trained BiLSTM-BAN
  protein-ligand model, it is fine-tuned on the growth hormone secretagogue
  receptor (GHSR) with 1,539 ligands and infers activation- versus
  inhibition-associated residues and their co-attention network topology
  without crystallographic priors.
